  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Reintegration of Sri Lankan Refugees Returnees from Tamil Nadu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project: Sustainable Reintegration of Sri Lankan Refugee Returnees from Tamil Nadu will be implemented by the International Organization for Migration (IOM) Sri Lanka with funding from and in coordination with the United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR.) The overall project objective is to facilitate sustainable reintegration of Sri Lankan refugees returning from Tamil Nadu in 2024. The project responds to ongoing needs due to the protracted conflict in Sri Lanka between 1983 to 2009. Sri Lankan refugees in the refugee camps in Tamil Nadu, India who opt to return to Sri Lanka, would require durable solutions/sustainable reintegration options upon their return. The project will aim to reach a maximum of 225 refugee returnees. The assistance will comprise the following: reintegration grants to refugee returnees, protection monitoring and provision of mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS). The project is pursuant to a formal request made by UNHCR in Sri Lanka for IOM to support reintegration of refugee returnees since UNHCR is in the process of downsizing its operations in the country.</narrative>
  </description>
